{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.GramDeterminantPlancherelRatio","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.GramDeterminantPlancherelRatio","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.EmSpectralCompleteness","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.ForceCarrierBringUniqueness"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.gram_kappa_numerical_value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.gram_kappa_numerical_value","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gram-determinant-plancherel-ratio.lean#L127-L164","doc":"**Numerical value of `κ` at the substrate** (open — stated, not proved).\n\nFor the genus-4 torus pair `T_{2,9}` (strong) and `T_{3,5}` (weak) at the\nsubstrate `q₀ ≈ 1.1097`, the Plancherel-weighted product is `≈ 1.722`.\n\nThe torus-pair data enters through `cs`, `cw` and the factorials.\n`CharacterDecomposition` is a formal placeholder over arbitrary\n`chi` / `dim_classical` / `dim_quantum`, so nothing in this file pins the\nknots — which is why the torus-pair condition is carried as an ABSTRACT\nPREDICATE parameter `IsTorusPairAtQ0` rather than as a construction.\n\n**Why not a `True` placeholder.** The first draft of this replacement wrote\nthe condition as `(h_torus_pair : True)`. That is not a weak hypothesis, it\nis NO hypothesis: `True` is supplied by `trivial`, so the statement it\nguards is logically `∀ cs cw, |gramKappa … − 1.722| < 0.001`, which is\nFALSE for generic character data (the product is unconstrained). Queuing a\nfalse proposition behind `sorry` is a worse defect than the provable axiom\nthis replaced — the axiom was redundant, a false `sorry` is a trap for\nwhoever tries to discharge it. Caught by reading the statement, not by any\ndetector; the `true-class-field` pattern of `proof-claims-unencoded` covers\nclass FIELDS typed `True`, not theorem HYPOTHESES typed `True`, so nothing\nin the audit would have flagged it. Recorded as a second blind spot.\n\n**What is open.** Nothing in this file constructs `IsTorusPairAtQ0`, so this\ntheorem has no instance and no consumer. Supplying that predicate — a\ntorus-knot character construction for `T_{2,9}` and `T_{3,5}` over the\n`CharacterDecomposition` placeholder — IS the open work, and it is upstream\nof discharging the `sorry`, not downstream of it. Unlike the superseded\naxiom, the conclusion here constrains `gramKappa`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.gram_determinant_plancherel_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.gram_determinant_plancherel_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gram-determinant-plancherel-ratio.lean#L48-L94","doc":"**Proposition (closed-form κ via Plancherel weights)**.\n\nThe Gram-determinant ratio appearing in the Chern-Simons descent\nis given by the Plancherel-weighted character product over\nWedderburn blocks `λ ⊢ n`, with no 2-jet hand calculation.\n\n**🛑 THE STATEMENT BELOW DOES NOT CARRY THAT CLAIM — flagged 2026-09-05,\nnot rewritten.** It concludes `∃ κ : ℝ, κ = gramKappa …`, which is true for\n*any* right-hand side whatsoever (`⟨a, rfl⟩`, verified) and says nothing\nabout the Chern–Simons Gram ratio. The docstring's content — that the CS\nratio EQUALS this product — needs a term denoting that ratio, and this file\nhas none; `gramKappa` is a definition, so \"something equals it\" is not a\ntheorem about it.\n\nLeft in place rather than restated because supplying that term is a design\ndecision in this arc's owner's hands, not a mechanical repair.\n\n**Correction (2026-09-05).** This said \"no detector flags this\", and that\nwas wrong — I asserted an absence without running the corpus-grep\nchecklist. `∃ x, x = e := ⟨e, rfl⟩` is a NAMED class with a DEDICATED\ndetector since 2026-08-07: `scripts/lean-vacuous-existential-audit.py`,\nwritten up in `docs/audits/2026-08-07-lean-vacuous-existential-audit.md`\n(17 found, and the ten then-live have since been drained).\n\nWhat is true is narrower and sharper. That detector could not see THIS\ndeclaration because its bound-variable pattern was `[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_']*`\n— ASCII-only — and this one binds `κ`. So it reported `0 candidates in 0\nfiles`, which reads as a clean corpus. Widening the pattern to Unicode on\nthe same tree the same day reports **8 in 3 files**, every one bound to a\nGreek name. Nothing had been drained; they had never been seen. The\ndetector is fixed and now carries a `--self-test` so a future narrowing\ncannot report zero silently.\n\nThe live audit (`content/pipeline/lean-vacuity-axiom-audit.ts`) still does\nnot flag this, and that part is correct as stated: its nearest criterion,\n`proof-no-unused-hypothesis-rfl`, needs an UNUSED binder, and every binder\nhere is consumed by `gramKappa n q_factorial n_factorial cs cw`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.gramKappa","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.gramKappa","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gram-determinant-plancherel-ratio.lean#L37-L46","doc":"The Plancherel-weighted character product. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.CharacterDecomposition.dim_quantum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.CharacterDecomposition.dim_quantum","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gram-determinant-plancherel-ratio.lean#L35-L35","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.CharacterDecomposition.dim_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.CharacterDecomposition.dim_classical","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gram-determinant-plancherel-ratio.lean#L34-L34","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.CharacterDecomposition.chi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.CharacterDecomposition.chi","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gram-determinant-plancherel-ratio.lean#L33-L33","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.CharacterDecomposition.partitions","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.CharacterDecomposition.partitions","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gram-determinant-plancherel-ratio.lean#L32-L32","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.CharacterDecomposition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.CharacterDecomposition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gram-determinant-plancherel-ratio.lean#L31-L31","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.CharacterDecomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.CharacterDecomposition","kind":"structure","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gram-determinant-plancherel-ratio.lean#L29-L35","doc":"A formal placeholder for the central-idempotent character\ncoefficients of a braid `β` in `H_n(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}